From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: World of Warcraft <warcraft@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:21:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Local realm sessions join the realm's Wine, which runs
 without a screen

A local realm's servers run by Wine with no screen, started by the app
(WinePrefixSetup prepares the container's prefix as the session's screen
does, with no Activity; its Box64 and environment the session's). A
realm's game session joins that Wine: it leaves the runtime folder (the
Wine server's socket and shared memory), the registry and the drives as
the realm's start made them, carries WINLATOR_SESSION in its programs'
environment, and its end ends those only, the realm running on. Leave
ends the session; it leaves Recents with it, the launcher in front. The
active-container link is replaced in one step, and left when it's
already that container.
